  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• To a medium bowl, add haloumi and cover with water to soak.\n• Boil the kettle. Place couscous, the salt and butter in a large heatproof bowl.\n• Add the boiling water (3/4 cup for 2P // 1 1/2 cups for 4P) and stir to combine. Immediately cover with a plate and leave for 5 mins. Fluff up with a fork and set aside.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6839322f42dc4b9281987f3a/step-1b5bd600.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, roughly chop tomato.\n• Using a vegetable peeler, peel carrot into ribbons Drain and rinse chickpeas.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6839322f42dc4b9281987f3a/step-4f6de110.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Drain haloumi and pat dry. Cut the haloumi into 1cm-thick slices.\n• Heat a drizzle of olive oil in a medium frying pan over medium-high heat.\n• Cook haloumi until golden brown, 1-2 mins each side. Transfer to a plate and cover to keep warm.\n• Return the frying pan to medium-high heat with a drizzle of olive oil.\n• Cook chickpeas, tossing, until tender, 2-3 mins.\n• Add tomato & herb seasoning and tomato paste, and cook until fragrant, 1 min.\n• Stir in the water and a pinch of brown sugar, and simmer until slightly thickened, 1 min. Season to taste.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6839322f42dc4b9281987f3a/step-f6424620.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Add tomato, carrot and salad leaves to the couscous. Add a drizzle of vinegar and olive oil. Toss to combine and season to taste.\n• Divide veggie couscous between bowls, then top with herby chickpeas and haloumi.\n• Crumble over fetta cubes. Dollop with yoghurt to serve.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/6839322f42dc4b9281987f3a/step-f8e1d030.jpeg"
    }
  ]
